# Run outputs are local by default. The exception is the conformal evidence bundle:
# the writeup states that every conformal number traces to a committed artifact, and
# a claim that traces to prose is an attestation rather than a check.
#
# The contents are excluded rather than the directory itself. Git will not descend
# into an excluded directory, so `!/artifacts/conformal/x.json` under a `/artifacts/`
# rule silently matches nothing -- the negation looks right and does nothing at all.
# Excluding `/artifacts/*` keeps the directory itself reachable so the re-inclusions
# below can fire. Verify with `git check-ignore -v` on a real path, never by reading
# this file and assuming.
#
# Text results only: no model binaries, no raw C-MAPSS, no derived data. Anything
# large or regenerable stays out and the writeup says how to rebuild it.
/artifacts/*
!/artifacts/conformal/
/artifacts/conformal/*
!/artifacts/conformal/*.json
!/artifacts/conformal/*.csv
!/artifacts/conformal/*.md
/checkpoints/
/runs/
/mlruns/
/wandb/
*.parquet
*.duckdb
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx

